MOON WITH A GUY,
INSTEAD OF JUST EMPTY.

00:22:59.077 --> 00:23:00.712 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
UNMANNED?

00:23:00.812 --> 00:23:02.947 line:0%
BUZZ ALDRIN: WE FIGURED
THEY WERE GOING TO PUT

00:23:03.047 --> 00:23:04.582 line:0%
A COSMONAUT IN HER.

00:23:04.682 --> 00:23:06.718 line:0%
SO WE ACCELERATED UH APOLLO 8.

00:23:06.818 --> 00:23:11.089 line:0%
ANYWAY, THE LANDERS COMING
OFF THE PRODUCTION LINE,

00:23:11.189 --> 00:23:14.893 line:0%
UH WERE HEAVY AT FIRST.

00:23:14.993 --> 00:23:18.163 line:0%
AND THE FIRST ONE WAS
GOING TO BE LIGHT ENOUGH WAS

00:23:18.263 --> 00:23:21.065 line:0%
GOING TO BE LEM-6.

00:23:21.165 --> 00:23:26.237 line:0%
AND IT WORKED OUT TO BE
APOLLO 12 IN MID-OCTOBER.

00:23:26.337 --> 00:23:29.007 line:0%
ALRIGHT NOW THE
MANAGER OF LEM-5.

00:23:29.107 --> 00:23:30.475 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
THAT'S YOUR "LEM,"

00:23:30.575 --> 00:23:31.876 line:0%
LUNAR EXCURSION MODULE.

00:23:31.976 --> 00:23:34.045 line:0%
BUZZ ALDRIN: YEAH,
HE WANTED HIS TO LAND.

00:23:34.145 --> 00:23:37.081 line:0%
AND HE WENT TO GEORGE LOW,
THE APOLLO PROGRAM HEAD.

00:23:37.181 --> 00:23:40.618 line:0%
AND HE SAID, "GEORGE IF UH,
IF I GET THE WEIGHT DOWN WILL

00:23:40.718 --> 00:23:47.025 line:0%
YOU GUARANTEE THAT MY LANDER
WILL UH BE A LANDING MISSION?"

00:23:48.126 --> 00:23:50.495 line:0%
GEORGE LOW, HEAD OF
APOLLO PROGRAM SAYS,

00:23:50.595 --> 00:23:53.665 line:0%
"WELL OF COURSE I WOULD
LIKE TO HAVE ANOTHER CHANCE.

00:23:53.765 --> 00:23:55.867 line:0%
AN EARLIER CHANCE TO LAND."

00:23:55.967 --> 00:24:01.972 line:0%
SO HE WENT AHEAD AND LEM-5
BECAME QUALIFIED AND WE LANDED.

00:24:02.840 --> 00:24:08.012 line:0%
INSTEAD OF PETE CONRAD
BEING THE FIRST ON THE MOON.

00:24:08.213 --> 00:24:09.648 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
I DID NOT KNOW THIS,

00:24:09.748 --> 00:24:10.849 line:0%
UNTIL HE TOLD ME THAT.

00:24:10.949 --> 00:24:13.150 line:0%
I DID NOT KNOW THAT
APOLLO 12 WAS SCHEDULED TO

00:24:13.250 --> 00:24:14.752 line:0%
BE THE FIRST MOON LANDING.

00:24:14.852 --> 00:24:17.322 line:0%
WITH PETE CONRAD, THE
FIRST TO STEP OFF THE LEM.

00:24:17.422 --> 00:24:19.724 line:0%
BECAUSE THAT WOULD HAVE BEEN
THE LEM LIGHT ENOUGH TO,

00:24:19.824 --> 00:24:24.128 line:0%
TO BE SERVED BY THE LIMIT,
LIMIT OF THE FUEL AVAILABLE TO

00:24:24.228 --> 00:24:25.997 line:0%
SEND IT BACK AND
COMPLETE THE MISSION.

00:24:26.097 --> 00:24:27.231 line:0%
MIKE MASSIMINO: RIGHT.

00:24:27.332 --> 00:24:28.532 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
SO THEY, THAT SOMEONE

00:24:28.632 --> 00:24:30.034 line:0%
WORKED ON THEIR LEM.

00:24:30.134 --> 00:24:31.336 line:0%
AND SLIPPED THEM IN AHEAD.

00:24:31.436 --> 00:24:33.104 line:0%
THAT, I MEAN THAT'S,
THAT'S, THAT'S.

00:24:33.204 --> 00:24:34.139 line:0%
MIKE MASSIMINO: AMAZING.

00:24:34.239 --> 00:24:35.473 line:0%
I DIDN'T KNOW THAT, EITHER.

00:24:35.574 --> 00:24:36.907 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
IT'S GANGSTER, THAT...

00:24:37.007 --> 00:24:38.409 line:0%
ILIZA SHLESINGER:
WHAT I GOT TO DO TO MAKE

00:24:38.509 --> 00:24:39.677 line:0%
MY LEM LAND FIRST.

00:24:39.777 --> 00:24:41.045 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
YEAH, YEAH, THAT'S SO GANGSTER.

00:24:41.145 --> 00:24:42.547 line:0%
ILIZA SHLESINGER:
SLIP THEM A 20, YEAH.

00:24:42.647 --> 00:24:44.315 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
THAT'S RIGHT, AND OF COURSE

00:24:44.416 --> 00:24:45.850 line:0%
WHAT'S HURRYING THIS
ALONG IS THAT WE HAVE A

00:24:45.950 --> 00:24:47.318 line:0%
SPACE RACE WITH
THE SOVIET UNION.

00:24:47.418 --> 00:24:49.420 line:0%
AND I DON'T KNOW HOW MUCH
PEOPLE REMEMBER ABOUT THAT.

00:24:49.520 --> 00:24:51.289 line:0%
MAY, MAYBE SOME OLD TIMERS DO,

00:24:51.389 --> 00:24:53.758 line:0%
BUT OTHERS MAYBE YOU
LEARNED ABOUT IT IN A BOOK.

00:24:53.858 --> 00:24:56.460 line:0%
BUT WE WERE IN COLD WAR
WITH THE SOVIET UNION.

00:24:56.560 --> 00:24:57.562 line:0%
THERE IT WAS.

00:24:57.662 --> 00:24:58.863 line:0%
OKAY?

00:24:58.963 --> 00:25:00.231 line:0%
AND IN THAT COLD WAR,

00:25:00.331 --> 00:25:02.967 line:0%
WE'RE BUILDING
UP OUR WEAPONS ARSENAL.

00:25:03.067 --> 00:25:06.037 line:0%
AND ONE KIND OF WEAPON,
WHICH WAS PARTICULARLY POTENT,

00:25:06.137 --> 00:25:08.873 line:0%
IS THE INTERCONTINENTAL
BALLISTIC MISSILE.

00:25:08.973 --> 00:25:10.541 line:0%
SO THIS IS A
MISSILE YOU LAUNCH,

00:25:10.641 --> 00:25:12.744 line:0%
AND IT LEAVES THE
ATMOSPHERE OF THE EARTH.

00:25:12.844 --> 00:25:16.180 line:0%
AND IT TRAVELS MOST OF
ITS DISTANCE SUB-ORBITAL,

00:25:16.281 --> 00:25:19.484 line:0%
THEN COMES OUT OF THE
ATMOSPHERE AND LANDS,

00:25:19.584 --> 00:25:21.653 line:0%
AND YOU WOULD LOAD THEM
WITH NUCLEAR WARHEADS,

00:25:21.753 --> 00:25:23.854 line:0%
AND IT CAN GO BETWEEN ANY
TWO POINTS ON EARTH WITHIN

00:25:23.954 --> 00:25:25.189 line:0%
FORTY-FIVE MINUTES.

00:25:25.289 --> 00:25:27.425 line:0%
YOU COULD NOT EVACUATE
A CITY IN TIME.

00:25:27.525 --> 00:25:29.427 line:0%
BECAUSE SUBORBITAL GETS
YOU HALFWAY AROUND THE EARTH

00:25:29.527 --> 00:25:30.995 line:0%
IN 45 MINUTES.

00:25:31.095 --> 00:25:33.498 line:0%
AND SO, SO
HERE'S WHAT HAPPENS.

00:25:33.598 --> 00:25:34.999 line:0%
JUST IN CASE YOU DON'T KNOW.

00:25:35.099 --> 00:25:39.070 line:0%
OCTOBER 4TH 1957,
RUSSIA LAUNCHES SPUTNIK.

00:25:39.170 --> 00:25:40.838 line:0%
AND YOU READ NORMAL
ACCOUNTS OF IT,

00:25:40.938 --> 00:25:42.406 line:0%
"OH IT'S THE FIRST
SPACE SATELLITE.

00:25:42.507 --> 00:25:44.342 line:0%
OKAY, THAT'S COOL."
IT STARTS THE SPACE RACE.

00:25:44.442 --> 00:25:46.844 line:0%
WHY DID WE FREAK OUT?

00:25:46.945 --> 00:25:49.614 line:0%
BECAUSE THAT WAS IN A
HOLLOWED OUT SHELL OF AN

00:25:49.714 --> 00:25:51.582 line:0%
INTERCONTINENTAL
BALLISTIC MISSILE!

00:25:51.682 --> 00:25:53.784 line:0%
AND IF THEY COULD FLY A
SATELLITE THAT WENT BEEP-BEEP

00:25:53.884 --> 00:25:56.654 line:0%
OVER OUR HEAD, THAT WAS
A, THAT WAS THE WRITING

00:25:56.754 --> 00:25:57.788 line:0%
ON THE WALL.

00:25:57.888 --> 00:26:00.258 line:0%
THAT WAS, THEY CAN SEND
ANYTHING OVER OUR HEAD.

00:26:00.358 --> 00:26:03.160 line:0%
AND WE WENT BALLISTIC.

00:26:03.260 --> 00:26:08.500 line:0%
AND WE, HA,HA, SO, SO
A, A YEAR AND A DAY LATER,

00:26:09.267 --> 00:26:10.802 line:0%
I'M BORN.

00:26:10.902 --> 00:26:12.637 line:0%
BUT THAT'S BESIDE THE POINT.

00:26:12.737 --> 00:26:15.840 line:0%
UH, A YEAR LATER THAT
WEEK, THE WEEK I WAS BORN,

00:26:15.940 --> 00:26:17.575 line:0%
NASA IS FOUNDED.

00:26:17.675 --> 00:26:18.809 line:0%
ILIZA SHLESINGER: WOW.

00:26:18.909 --> 00:26:20.545 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
AND THAT BIRTHS OUR SPACE,

00:26:20.645 --> 00:26:22.046 line:0%
OUR PARTICIPATION
IN THE SPACE RACE.

00:26:22.146 --> 00:26:25.650 line:0%
SO, SO THEN WE ACTUALLY
LAUNCHED THE RACE TO THE MOON

00:26:25.750 --> 00:26:27.285 line:0%
WITH JFK'S SPEECH.

00:26:27.385 --> 00:26:29.153 line:0%
BECAUSE RUSSIA BEAT US
IN ALMOST EVERYTHING ELSE,

00:26:29.254 --> 00:26:30.989 line:0%
AND HE THINKS MAYBE WE
CAN BEAT THEM IN GETTING

00:26:31.089 --> 00:26:31.989 line:0%
TO THE MOON.

00:26:32.089 --> 00:26:33.324 line:0%
SO WE LAUNCHED THAT.

00:26:33.424 --> 00:26:35.393 line:0%
SO THE, THAT'S THE, THAT'S
THE STORY IN A NUTSHELL.

00:26:35.493 --> 00:26:37.394 line:0%
AND WE HAVE THE MERCURY
PROGRAM, THE GEMINI PROGRAM.

00:26:37.495 --> 00:26:39.931 line:0%
MERCURY HOLDS ONE
ASTRONAUT, GEMINI HOLDS TWO,

00:26:40.031 --> 00:26:41.432 line:0%
GEMINI TWINS, OF COURSE.

00:26:41.532 --> 00:26:43.401 line:0%
UH, APOLLO HOLDS THREE.

00:26:43.501 --> 00:26:44.802 line:0%
AND THERE YOU HAVE IT.

00:26:44.902 --> 00:26:47.505 line:0%
BUT DURING THAT APOLLO ERA,
WE WERE SPENDING MORE THAN

00:26:47.605 --> 00:26:49.573 line:0%
4% OF THE FEDERAL
BUDGET GOING INTO SPACE,

00:26:49.674 --> 00:26:51.842 line:0%
NOW IT'S ONE HALF OF
1% OF THE FEDERAL BUDGET.

00:26:51.942 --> 00:26:53.745 line:0%
SO THE VALUATION IS WAY LOWER.

00:26:53.845 --> 00:26:55.479 line:0%
BUT WE DID MANAGE
TO DO OTHER THINGS.

00:26:55.579 --> 00:26:57.716 line:0%
WE HAD SKYLAB, WE
HAD THE APOLLO SOYUZ.

00:26:57.816 --> 00:26:59.717 line:0%
UH, THE SOYUZ IS
THE RUSSIAN CAPSULE.

00:26:59.817 --> 00:27:01.452 line:0%
THEY, THEY CONNECTED,
REMEMBER THAT?

00:27:01.552 --> 00:27:02.854 line:0%
MIKE MASSIMINO:
YEAH. I REMEMBER THAT.

00:27:02.954 --> 00:27:04.488 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON: AND
OF COURSE, THE SPACE STATION.

00:27:04.588 --> 00:27:05.657 line:0%
DID YOU EVER GET TO
THE SPACE STATION?

00:27:05.757 --> 00:27:06.824 line:0%
MIKE MASSIMINO: I'VE NEVER
BEEN TO THE SPACE STATION.

00:27:06.924 --> 00:27:07.992 line:0%
ILIZA SHLESINGER:
OH, YOU HAVE TO GO.

00:27:08.092 --> 00:27:09.160 line:0%
MIKE MASSIMINO: REALLY?

00:27:09.260 --> 00:27:10.228 line:0%
ILIZA SHLESINGER: MUST GO.

00:27:10.328 --> 00:27:11.462 line:0%
MIKE MASSIMINO:
WHY, WHAT'S IT LIKE?

00:27:11.562 --> 00:27:12.663 line:0%
ILIZA SHLESINGER:
GO IN THE SPRING.

00:27:12.763 --> 00:27:13.832 line:0%
MIKE MASSIMINO:
HOW'S THE FOOD?

00:27:13.932 --> 00:27:14.899 line:0%
ILIZA SHLESINGER: IT'S
AMAZING, EVERYTHING'S FRESH.

00:27:14.999 --> 00:27:16.434 line:0%
MIKE MASSIMINO: GOOD SERVICE?

00:27:16.534 --> 00:27:17.936 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON: SO.

00:27:18.036 --> 00:27:20.872 line:0%
COMING UP AFTER THE BREAK,
MORE OF MY INTERVIEW WITH

00:27:20.972 --> 00:27:23.875 line:0%
MOONWALKER,
NATIONAL TREASURE,

00:27:23.975 --> 00:27:25.944 line:0%
BUZZ ALDRIN WHEN
STARTALK CONTINUES.

00:27:26.044 --> 00:27:29.614 line:0%
<i> [AUDIENCE APPLAUSE].</i>

00:27:35.019 --> 00:27:36.654 line:0%
<i> [AUDIENCE APPLAUSE].</i>

00:27:36.754 --> 00:27:38.289 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
WE'RE BACK ON STARTALK.

00:27:38.390 --> 00:27:40.124 line:0%
HERE AT THE ROSE CENTER
FOR EARTH AND SPACE.

00:27:40.224 --> 00:27:42.794 line:0%
AND WE'RE TALKING ABOUT
THE HISTORIC MISSION TO PUT

00:27:42.894 --> 00:27:44.395 line:0%
A MAN ON THE MOON.

00:27:44.495 --> 00:27:45.930 line:0%
AND BACK THEN IN
THE AGE OF APOLLO,

00:27:46.030 --> 00:27:49.834 line:0%
GREAT RISKS WERE TAKEN
FOR GREAT REWARDS.

00:27:50.501 --> 00:27:54.405 line:0%
AND I WONDERED TODAY,
IS THAT SAME RISK REWARD

00:27:54.505 --> 00:27:57.175 line:0%
RATIO STILL IN EFFECT?

00:27:57.875 --> 00:28:01.378 line:0%
AND I ASKED APOLLO 11 PILOT,
BUZZ ALDRIN ALL ABOUT IT,

00:28:01.478 --> 00:28:03.914 line:0%
LET'S CHECK IT OUT.

00:28:04.015 --> 00:28:06.017 line:0%
WE'RE IN A CULTURE NOW
WHERE EVERYONE IS AFRAID

00:28:06.117 --> 00:28:07.819 line:0%
TO MAKE A MISTAKE.

00:28:07.919 --> 00:28:09.954 line:0%
BECAUSE SOMETHING GOES
WRONG AND THEN SOMEBODY

00:28:10.054 --> 00:28:11.989 line:0%
HAS TO HAND OUT BLAME.

00:28:12.090 --> 00:28:14.992 line:0%
AND I WORRY THAT WE LIVE
IN A TIME VERY DIFFERENT

00:28:15.092 --> 00:28:17.995 line:0%
FROM WHEN I GREW UP, WHEN
WE'RE SENDING YOU TO THE MOON.

00:28:18.096 --> 00:28:21.933 line:0%
WHERE WE'RE NOT GOING
TO DISCOVER ANYTHING,

00:28:22.033 --> 00:28:25.402 line:0%
BECAUSE PEOPLE ARE GUN SHY,
EXPLORATION SHY, RISK DIVERSE.

00:28:25.669 --> 00:28:27.305 line:0%
BUZZ ALDRIN:
YEAH, UH, THERE'S,

00:28:27.405 --> 00:28:31.776 line:0%
THERE'S AN ENGINEER WHO'S
MADE KIND OF A SPECIALTY OF

00:28:31.876 --> 00:28:37.449 line:0%
UH OF REALLY ANALYZING HOW
MUCH IT COST US TO BE SO

00:28:39.317 --> 00:28:41.686 line:0%
SURE THAT
SOMETHING WON'T FAIL.

00:28:41.786 --> 00:28:44.789 line:0%
WE SPEND SO MUCH
MONEY TO DO THAT.

00:28:44.889 --> 00:28:47.425 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
WE SPEND MONEY TO NOT FAIL.

00:28:47.525 --> 00:28:49.627 line:0%
BUZZ ALDRIN: A LOT, OH YEAH.

00:28:49.727 --> 00:28:51.829 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON: NOT,
NOT REALIZING THE VALUE OF

00:28:51.929 --> 00:28:53.431 line:0%
FAILURE IN THE FIRST PLACE.

00:28:53.531 --> 00:28:55.300 line:0%
SO MAYBE NASA NEEDS
A SKUNK WORKS.

00:28:55.400 --> 00:28:56.600 line:0%
THEY NEED A, A...

00:28:56.701 --> 00:28:58.869 line:0%
BUZZ ALDRIN: WELL WE GOT
ONE, WE GOT ONE DOWN,

00:28:58.969 --> 00:29:00.104 line:0%
DOWN IN FLORIDA.

00:29:00.205 --> 00:29:02.273 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON: WHERE?

00:29:02.373 --> 00:29:04.275 line:0%
BUZZ ALDRIN: YOU KNOW,
THEY GOT ALLIGATORS AND STUFF.

00:29:04.375 --> 00:29:05.977 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON: WHAT?

00:29:06.077 --> 00:29:08.212 line:0%
BUZZ ALDRIN: BUT, BUT
THIS IS KENNEDY SPACE CENTER

00:29:08.312 --> 00:29:11.015 line:0%
AND THEY HAVE A SWAMP WORKS.

00:29:11.115 --> 00:29:12.616 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON: SO
IF YOUR, IF YOUR LAUNCH FAILS...

00:29:12.717 --> 00:29:14.084 line:0%
YOU GET EATEN BY
ALLIGATOR, OKAY.

00:29:14.184 --> 00:29:17.154 line:0%
BUZZ ALDRIN:
THERE'S SWAMP WORKS, OKAY?

00:29:17.255 --> 00:29:20.324 line:0%
DOWN WHERE THE ALLIGATORS
ARE, THERE'S SWAMPS.

00:29:20.424 --> 00:29:23.060 line:0%
AND THEY ARE UH
GETTING INTO SOME...

00:29:23.160 --> 00:29:25.396 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
SO THIS IS REAL?

00:29:25.496 --> 00:29:27.098 line:0%
BUZZ ALDRIN: ABSOLUTELY.

00:29:27.198 --> 00:29:28.233 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
YOU KNOW, I DIDN'T KNOW

00:29:28.333 --> 00:29:29.767 line:0%
ABOUT THE SWAMP WORKS.

00:29:29.867 --> 00:29:32.603 line:0%
ONE OF THE, ONE OF BUZZ'S
FAVORITE QUOTES IS A VARIANT

00:29:32.703 --> 00:29:35.973 line:0%
ON THE ONE WE ALL LEARNED
FROM THE APOLLO 13 MOVIE.

00:29:36.074 --> 00:29:37.876 line:0%
MIKE MASSIMINO:
"FAILURE IS NOT AN OPTION."

00:29:37.976 --> 00:29:39.710 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
"FAILURE IS NOT AN OPTION."

00:29:39.810 --> 00:29:41.979 line:0%
AND BUZZ HAS A
DIFFERENT TAKE ON THAT.

00:29:42.079 --> 00:29:45.282 line:0%
IN HIS BOOK HE SAYS, "NO,
FAILURE IS ALWAYS AN OPTION."

00:29:46.117 --> 00:29:48.286 line:0%
UH, ONE OF THE LESSONS HE
DESCRIBES IN THAT BOOK.

00:29:48.386 --> 00:29:50.788 line:0%
BECAUSE IF FAILURE
IS NOT AN OPTION,

00:29:50.888 --> 00:29:53.324 line:0%
THEN YOU'RE AT RISK
OF BEING TOO SAFE.

00:29:53.424 --> 00:29:56.094 line:0%
AND IN FACT,
LOCKHEED MARTIN AND,

00:29:56.194 --> 00:29:57.761 line:0%
THE PENTAGON AND OTHERS
HAVE GOTTEN TOGETHER.

00:29:57.862 --> 00:29:59.497 line:0%
SO THEY HAD WHAT WAS
CALLED THE SKUNK WORKS.

00:29:59.597 --> 00:30:06.070 line:0%
WHERE THEY UH WOULD DESIGN
ADVANCED UH AVIATION ELEMENTS.

00:30:06.537 --> 00:30:10.141 line:0%
AND OUT OF THAT CAME
THINGS LIKE STEALTH AND UH

00:30:10.241 --> 00:30:12.343 line:0%
VERY HIGH SPEED CRAFT.

00:30:12.443 --> 00:30:13.844 line:0%
YOU KNOW, HIGH MACH NUMBER.

00:30:13.944 --> 00:30:16.080 line:0%
UH, MULTIPLE TIMES THE
SPEED OF SOUND AND,

00:30:16.180 --> 00:30:19.750 line:0%
AND IN THAT GROUP, THEY
HAD VERY LITTLE OVERSIGHT.

00:30:19.850 --> 00:30:21.786 line:0%
VERY LITTLE MANAGEMENT
TELLING THEM WHAT

00:30:21.886 --> 00:30:23.988 line:0%
BOTTOM LINE TO, TO MATCH.

00:30:24.088 --> 00:30:26.157 line:0%
AND ONLY THEN DID I JUST
LEARN THAT NASA HAS THAT.

00:30:26.257 --> 00:30:27.692 line:0%
I'M, I'M ASHAMED,
I DIDN'T KNOW THIS.

00:30:27.792 --> 00:30:28.893 line:0%
THE, THE SWAMP WORKS.

00:30:28.993 --> 00:30:30.261 line:0%
DID YOU KNOW ABOUT
THE SWAMP WORKS?

00:30:30.361 --> 00:30:32.196 line:0%
MIKE MASSIMINO: YOU KNOW I,
I HAD A STUDENT A COUPLE

00:30:32.297 --> 00:30:33.364 line:0%
YEARS AGO THAT HAD
A SUMMER INTERNSHIP THERE.

00:30:33.464 --> 00:30:34.699 line:0%
SO I, I LEARNED
ABOUT IT THROUGH HIM.

00:30:34.799 --> 00:30:36.234 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
UH-HUH, DO YOU REMEMBER WHAT

00:30:36.334 --> 00:30:37.468 line:0%
STUFF THEY WERE DOING?

00:30:37.569 --> 00:30:38.869 line:0%
MIKE MASSIMINO:
THEY WERE DOING SOME REALLY

00:30:38.969 --> 00:30:39.971 line:0%
COOL ROBOTIC STUFF.

00:30:40.071 --> 00:30:41.139 line:0%
SOME LIKE CUTTING EDGE,
COOL ROBOTIC STUFF THAT.

00:30:41.239 --> 00:30:42.540 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
WITHOUT SOME MANAGER COMING

00:30:42.640 --> 00:30:44.174 line:0%
OVER SAY, "YOU GOT
TO MAKE THE BOTTOM LINE."

00:30:44.275 --> 00:30:45.342 line:0%
MIKE MASSIMINO: UH,
I, I THINK THAT'S WHAT,

00:30:45.442 --> 00:30:46.678 line:0%
THAT WAS THE IDEA,
DO SOME EXCITING STUFF, YEAH.

00:30:46.778 --> 00:30:47.878 line:0%
ILIZA SHLESINGER:
IT'S A THINK TANK.

