00:41:27.584 --> 00:41:28.952 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
THERE'S A BACKDOOR.

00:41:29.052 --> 00:41:30.220 line:0%
MIKE MASSIMINO: I THINK
THAT'S WHAT'S WHAT, YEAH.

00:41:30.320 --> 00:41:31.622 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
THAT KIND OF...

00:41:31.722 --> 00:41:32.990 line:0%
ILIZA SHLESINGER: SLIP THE
SECURITY GUARD SOMETHING.

00:41:33.090 --> 00:41:34.424 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
YEAH THEY, DIDN'T SHOW THE,

00:41:34.524 --> 00:41:35.726 line:0%
THEY DIDN'T SHOW THE...

00:41:35.826 --> 00:41:37.293 line:0%
ILIZA SHLESINGER: NO ONE
THERE, HE WENT ON A SUNDAY.

00:41:37.393 --> 00:41:38.895 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON: YEAH,
YEAH, YEAH, WENT ON A SUNDAY.

00:41:38.995 --> 00:41:40.196 line:0%
SO, SO WHAT ARE YOUR
PARTING REFLECTIONS, ILIZA?

00:41:40.297 --> 00:41:42.132 line:0%
ILIZA SHLESINGER: I
THINK WITHOUT DREAMERS,

00:41:42.232 --> 00:41:43.366 line:0%
WE WOULD NEVER GET
TO OUTER SPACE.

00:41:43.466 --> 00:41:46.937 line:0%
SO I THINK THE MORE WE CAN
ENCOURAGE PEOPLE TO DREAM NO

00:41:47.037 --> 00:41:50.206 line:0%
MATTER HOW SILLY, OR
STUPID, OR INSANE IT SOUNDS,

00:41:50.306 --> 00:41:52.810 line:0%
NOBODY'S CALLED
CRAZY WHEN THEY ACTUALLY

00:41:52.910 --> 00:41:54.177 line:0%
SUCCEED AT SOMETHING.

00:41:54.278 --> 00:41:55.912 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
ANYONE WHO SUCCEEDS IS

00:41:56.012 --> 00:41:56.947 line:0%
NEVER CALLED CRAZY.

00:41:57.047 --> 00:41:58.148 line:0%
I LIKE THAT.

00:41:58.248 --> 00:41:59.216 line:0%
SO, SO MIKE?

00:41:59.316 --> 00:42:00.384 line:0%
YEAH, GIVE ME SOMETHING.

00:42:00.484 --> 00:42:01.852 line:0%
MIKE MASSIMINO:
I, I THINK IT'S VERY...

00:42:01.952 --> 00:42:03.654 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON: THE
OLD MAN WHO HAS BEEN IN SPACE.

00:42:03.754 --> 00:42:04.889 line:0%
MIKE MASSIMINO: YEAH.

00:42:04.989 --> 00:42:06.557 line:0%
I, I THINK, I THINK IT'S
GREAT THAT YOU HAD BUZZ ON.

00:42:06.657 --> 00:42:07.757 line:0%
BECAUSE HE'S REALLY
A NATIONAL TREASURE.

00:42:07.857 --> 00:42:09.793 line:0%
TWELVE, ONLY TWELVE PEOPLE
GOT TO WALK ON THE MOON.

00:42:09.893 --> 00:42:11.928 line:0%
UH, SEVEN OF THEM ARE STILL
AROUND, AND IT'S GREAT TO,

00:42:12.028 --> 00:42:13.797 line:0%
TO HAVE HIM
FEATURED LIKE THAT.

00:42:13.897 --> 00:42:15.932 line:0%
UM, WHAT THEY
ACCOMPLISHED WAS GREAT,

00:42:16.032 --> 00:42:17.601 line:0%
BUT IT WAS A BLIP, RIGHT?

00:42:17.701 --> 00:42:19.169 line:0%
IT HAPPENED, IT WAS
A LONG TIME AGO,

00:42:19.269 --> 00:42:20.537 line:0%
WE WENT THERE AND CAME BACK.

00:42:20.638 --> 00:42:22.239 line:0%
AND THE NEXT TIME WE GO,
I THINK WE SHOULD SETTLE

00:42:22.339 --> 00:42:23.540 line:0%
IN A LITTLE MORE.

00:42:23.640 --> 00:42:24.642 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
SETTLE IN.

00:42:24.742 --> 00:42:26.043 line:0%
YOU MEAN UH,
CREATE A MOON COLONY?

00:42:26.143 --> 00:42:28.178 line:0%
MIKE MASSIMINO: CREATE
A COLONY, A SETTLEMENT,

00:42:28.278 --> 00:42:30.247 line:0%
A PLACE TO HANG OUT.

00:42:30.347 --> 00:42:32.115 line:0%
RESEARCH LABORATORY,
WHATEVER YOU WANT TO CALL IT.

00:42:32.215 --> 00:42:34.451 line:0%
I THINK WE SHOULD
GO AND STAY FOREVER.

00:42:34.551 --> 00:42:36.619 line:0%
DR. NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON:
SO WHEN I THINK ABOUT ALL

00:42:36.719 --> 00:42:39.623 line:0%
THIS AND REFLECT,
UH I THINK TO MYSELF,

00:42:39.723 --> 00:42:42.426 line:0%
THERE IS AN OUTER SPACE
TREATY FOR THE PEACEFUL USE

00:42:42.526 --> 00:42:44.060 line:0%
OF OUTER SPACE.

00:42:44.160 --> 00:42:46.329 line:0%
SO THE GOAL IS WHEN
WE ALL GO INTO SPACE,

00:42:46.429 --> 00:42:48.598 line:0%
WE WILL TREAT ONE
ANOTHER KINDLY.

00:42:48.698 --> 00:42:50.100 line:0%
AND I DON'T HAVE THE
CONFIDENCE THAT OTHERS

00:42:50.200 --> 00:42:51.501 line:0%
HAVE IN THAT.

00:42:51.601 --> 00:42:54.604 line:0%
I WANT TO BELIEVE IT,
BUT I SAY TO MYSELF IF YOU

00:42:54.704 --> 00:42:57.708 line:0%
CAN TREAT EACH
OTHER KINDLY IN SPACE,

00:42:58.942 --> 00:43:01.044 line:0%
THEN WHY NOT
DO THAT HERE ON EARTH?

00:43:01.144 --> 00:43:04.781 line:0%
WHY DO YOU HAVE TO BE IN
SPACE TO NOT KILL ONE ANOTHER?

00:43:04.881 --> 00:43:07.417 line:0%
HOWEVER, MY ONE
GLIMMER OF HOPE,

00:43:07.517 --> 00:43:10.320 line:0%
IS THAT SO MUCH OF HUMAN
CONFLICT IN THE HISTORY OF

00:43:10.420 --> 00:43:14.624 line:0%
CIVILIZATION HAS BEEN DERIVED
FROM SCARCITY OF RESOURCES,

00:43:14.724 --> 00:43:17.060 line:0%
AND ACCESS TO THOSE RESOURCES.

00:43:17.160 --> 00:43:18.829 line:0%
AND I LOOK AT SPACE.

00:43:18.929 --> 00:43:20.831 line:0%
ASTEROIDS, COMETS.

00:43:20.931 --> 00:43:24.134 line:0%
STARS WITH LIMITLESS
ENERGY, AND I REALIZE,

00:43:24.234 --> 00:43:28.906 line:0%
WE SHOULD ALL REALIZE, THAT
SPACE IS A LIMITLESS SUPPLY OF

00:43:30.073 --> 00:43:31.908 line:0%
NATURAL RESOURCES.

00:43:32.008 --> 00:43:35.979 line:0%
SPACE MAY BE THE ONLY PLACE
WHERE PEACE IS GUARANTEED,

00:43:37.080 --> 00:43:40.350 line:0%
BECAUSE IN FACT, WE WOULD
HAVE RUN OUT OF ALL REASONS

00:43:40.450 --> 00:43:42.719 line:0%
FOR WHY TO KILL ONE ANOTHER.

00:43:42.819 --> 00:43:44.988 line:0%
YOU'VE BEEN WATCHING STARTALK,

00:43:45.088 --> 00:43:47.090 line:0%
HERE AT THE AMERICAN
MUSEUM OF NATURAL HISTORY.

00:43:47.190 --> 00:43:49.392 line:0%
AND I'VE BEEN YOUR HOST,
YOUR PERSONAL ASTROPHYSICIST,

00:43:49.492 --> 00:43:50.794 line:0%
NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON.

00:43:50.894 --> 00:43:54.131 line:0%
AND AS ALWAYS, I NOW BID
ALL OF YOU, NOT ONLY FAREWELL,

00:43:54.231 --> 00:43:59.169 line:0%
BUT I REQUIRE IN LIFE
THAT YOU KEEP LOOKING UP.

00:43:59.269 --> 00:44:03.107 line:0%
<i> [AUDIENCE APPLAUSE].</i>

